# What this repository does NOT carry.

# Build output. The panel's source is committed; its target directory is not, and it holds
# absolute paths from whichever box last built it.
target/

# Machine-local runtime: logs, worktrees, leases, cockpit state. Regenerated, and none of it
# is content.
.runtime/

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The operator's own configuration — real paths, real repositories, real personas. The
# examples ship; these do not, and keeping them untracked is what lets the harness be
# shared at all.
#
# `repo-map` is here rather than only `repo-map.local` because conf.sh resolves the map in
# the order config-dir, `$SPIRA_HOME/repo-map`, `repo-map.example` — so a tracked map at the
# second position is not dead weight a colleague ignores, it is the map their clone silently
# USES, naming checkouts they do not have.
/spira.conf
spira/repo-map
spira/repo-map.local

# Wiki content belongs to the brain repository, not to the harness. An aeon working in a
# spira-harness worktree that also runs sop.sh synth or writes a note must write to
# $SPIRA_WIKI, not relative to its cwd. This entry ensures a misdirected write stays
# untracked rather than landing on main — the fence that turns the mistake into a miss
# rather than an inventory refusal.
wiki/

# A groom pass's findings belong in bd notes on its trigger bead and in
# $SPIRA_RUN/groom.log, never in a file every branch would share and conflict on.
.groom-findings.txt

# Editor and OS litter.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# --- beads data: never in a shared repository (exclude.sh) ------------------------------
# A beads database holds internal working notes, agent memories and the overseer's own
# judgement. It belongs to whoever runs the harness, is never public, and is in no shared
# repository. `*.jsonl` is here because `bd export` writes one, and an export of the
# issues is the database in the form that needs no tooling at all to read.
.beads/
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key
.beads.gate.lock
*.jsonl
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
